AadhaarMethodValidateTrustedKeysTest
├── when the constructor gets one nonzero word
│   └── it should store it as the one trusted word.
├── when the constructor gets a zero word
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry AadhaarMethod_ZeroTrustedKey of index zero.
├── when the constructor gets an empty list
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of zero.
├── when the constructor gets two words
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of two.
├── when the constructor gets any length but one
│   ├── it should revert.
│   └── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of that length.
├── when the key admin sets one nonzero word
│   ├── it should emit TrustedKeysUpdated from the previous key to the new one.
│   └── it should store the new key as the one trusted word.
├── when the key admin sets one nonzero word twice in a row
│   └── it should store the second key as the one trusted word.
├── when the key admin sets an empty list
│   ├── it should revert.
│   ├── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of zero.
│   └── it should keep the previous key.
├── when the key admin sets two words
│   ├── it should revert.
│   ├── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of two.
│   └── it should keep the previous key.
├── when the key admin sets any length but one
│   ├── it should revert.
│   ├── it should carry AadhaarMethod_InvalidTrustedKeysLength of that length.
│   └── it should keep the previous key.
└── when the key admin sets a zero word
    ├── it should revert.
    ├── it should carry AadhaarMethod_ZeroTrustedKey of index zero.
    └── it should keep the previous key.
